# "Missed you" greetings (T-108): played once when the player talks to a villager after a week or more away (hearts 2 and up).
# The return is also worth a few friendship points (WarmthModel). One line each; voice rules apply to the locked villagers.

say npc.wren.missed wren: There you are! A whole week without a word. I nearly told the stool your secrets just to have someone to tell.
say npc.hazel.missed hazel: Oh. You're back. (I kept your chair. It stayed empty. It was very polite about it.) I'm glad.
say npc.bram.missed bram: ...Hm. A week. Forge was quiet. Hm. Good to see you.
say npc.tilda.missed tilda: There you are! I kept your page on the slate warm. The shop's been quiet without you. Mind the cat.
say npc.juno.missed juno: Okay, okay, okay, you're back! I made a clasp for every day you were gone. The pile's a bit embarrassing.
say npc.piper.missed piper: A week! I wrote you a verse for every night. Most are bad. One is about soup. That's a chorus.
say npc.marcus.missed marcus: Ah. You're back. The workshop's been quiet. I planed a plank twice, just to hear the sound.
say npc.odalys.missed odalys: Welcome back. I trust you've been well. The clinic noticed your absence, in a clinical sort of way.
say npc.felix.missed felix: There you are. The fish were asking after you. Or I was. Hard to tell, at that hour.
say npc.ione.missed ione: Oh, hello again. I kept your place in the book. Nobody read ahead. I checked the margins.
say npc.dorian.missed dorian: ...You returned. I had a small mushroom for you, and then I ate it. I'll find another.
say npc.elara.missed elara: Back at last. I've kept a list of questions for you. It's become a short book.
